    "title": "Junior Radiologist at AIIMS Delhi",
    "description": "Join the AIIMS Delhi family as a Radiologist in Noida. We believe in empowering our employees with the tools, training, and environment they need to succeed.\n\nAbout AIIMS Delhi:\nAIIMS Delhi is a leading organization in the Hybrid sector, committed to excellence, innovation, and employee growth. We offer a dynamic work environment where talent is recognized and rewarded.\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n• Administer medications and treatments as prescribed\n• Educate patients and families on health management and disease prevention\n• Provide high-quality patient care and maintain patient records\n• Maintain sterile environments and follow infection control protocols\n• Participate in quality improvement initiatives and clinical audits\n• Ensure patient privacy and maintain confidentiality\n• Monitor patient progress and adjust treatment plans accordingly\n\nRequired Skills & Qualifications:\n• CA / CMA / CFA certification\n• 10-15 years of relevant experience\n• Proficiency in Surgical Procedures\n• Proficiency in Telemedicine\n• Proficiency in NABH Standards\n• Proficiency in Wound Care\n• Proficiency in CPT Codes\n• Proficiency in HIPAA Compliance\n• Proficiency in ICD-10\n• Proficiency in Infection Control\n\nWork Mode: Hybrid - Flexible work-from-home and office\n\nWhat We Offer:\n• Work-from-home flexibility\n• Company-sponsored certifications\n• Employee stock options (ESOPs) for eligible roles\n• Modern office with recreational facilities\n• Life and accident insurance\n• Competitive salary with performance-linked incentives\n• Salary Range: 20 LPA - 40 LPA per annum\n\nLocation: Noida, Uttar Pradesh, India\n\nIf you are excited about this opportunity, apply now and take the next step in your career journey with AIIMS Delhi!",
